  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a4da58d2dc2409c459ef20449bf92a90, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tension
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lessonId: What is Tension
  lessonTitle: What is Tension
  lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
  lessonDescription: "Tension is a pulling force that stretches a structural member.\nWhen
    a member is under tension, forces pull away from each other at opposite ends.
    The member becomes slightly longer as it carries the load. If the tension becomes
    greater than the material\u2019s strength, the member may stretch excessively
    or break.\nCables, ropes, and the lower portions of some bridge components commonly
    resist tension.\nBridge Example:\nThe main cables of a suspension bridge are
    placed under tension as they support the bridge deck."
